# Sensor classifier model card: sensor_v2.keras and sensor_v2_no_stage.keras

> **Simulated data.** Data: {{models/mlp_sensor/manifest.json::data}}. The results below show that the training and evaluation pipeline works. They do not show that the model works on real sensors.

## Purpose
Classifies one sensor reading as normal or one of three stress classes. Fusion does not use single readings: `fusion/sensor_window.py` aggregates the labels over a 24-hour window.

## Version and files
- Version: {{models/mlp_sensor/manifest.json::version}}
- Full model (with growth stage): {{models/mlp_sensor/manifest.json::file}} ({{models/mlp_sensor/manifest.json::bytes}} bytes), sha256 {{models/mlp_sensor/manifest.json::sha256}}
- No-stage model (used {{models/mlp_sensor/manifest.json::input.use_no_stage_file_when}}): {{models/mlp_sensor/manifest.json::no_stage_file}} ({{models/mlp_sensor/manifest.json::no_stage_bytes}} bytes), sha256 {{models/mlp_sensor/manifest.json::no_stage_sha256}}
